I'm not sure if this fix everything, but at least this part of the Ravi's model is problematic:

    vector<lower=0>[J] sigma ;      // scale of multivariate vector
    vector<lower=0>[J] nu ;
    ...
    sigma[j] ~ uniform(0,100) ;
    nu[j] ~ uniform(4,30) ;

The problem is that Stan is generating parameters outside of the support of parameters (that is, from interval (0, inf) and not (0,100) and (4,30)). Easy fix would be to declare parameters as (impling the same uniform prior as in the original model, no need to explicitly write them down):

    vector<lower=0,upper=100>[J] sigma ;      // scale of multivariate vector
    vector<lower=4,upper=30>[J] nu ;

